{
  "_comment": "Mot Dang basemap style over the Protomaps v4 vector schema. Printed-map ground like the front page (blue water, green parks, softer forest, relief, landmark badges, road shields), high-contrast pins drawn ON TOP by each layer module — nothing in here competes with a pin. Palette is the site's: cream paper #FBF6EC, rule #BCA070, moat blue #8FA5CC, ant red #D4552C. Source id is 'p', set by map_shell.py. Symbol (label) layers are dropped automatically when no self-hosted glyph URL is configured — see map_shell.emit().",
  "_labels": "Thai first, Latin second, on two lines. NOTE: the Protomaps v4 schema carries no name:th — verified against the built archive. 'name' IS the local name, which in this bbox is the Thai one, and 'name:en' is the Latin. Asking for name:th returns nothing and every label silently falls through to English, which on a Thai-first site is exactly backwards.",
